# AI use policy

scikit-image's own policy (`CONTRIBUTING.md`, "AI Policy") is the model for Acme's. The human author must fully understand and own every change.

## The agent may
- Explore and explain the codebase, conventions, and history.
- Do mechanical changes (removing a completed deprecation, applying a decorator across modules, renames).
- Iterate on code the engineer wrote; fix trivial bugs.
- Write test **scaffolding** and fix broken tests.
- Write CI and infrastructure code that is easy to review.
- Review a diff against these rules and list problems.

## The agent should not, on its own
- Write novel algorithmic code. Explain the approach and let the engineer write it, or pair on it.
- Decide what to test. Propose edge cases with a one-line reason each; the engineer chooses.
- Write the PR description or review comments as if from the engineer. It may draft a checklist the engineer rewrites.

## Every AI-assisted change
- Keep AI-generated changes in separate commits where practical.
- Add an `Assisted-by: Cursor <model>` trailer to those commits.
- Say in the PR description which parts used AI.
- AI-generated code must be trivial to review. If it isn't, split it or hand it back to the engineer.
